abola $(y-1)^{2}=5(x+7)?$" :question/worked-solution "The standard equation of a left- or right-opening parabola that has its vertex at $(h,k)$ is\n\n$$\n(y-k)^{2}=4p(x-h),\n$$\n\nwhere $p$ is constant.\n\nWe can rewrite the given equation as \n\n$$\n(y-1)^{2}=4(\\frac{5}{4})(x+7).\n$$\n\nIt is now clear that our equation is of the standard type with $p=\\frac{5}{4}.$ \n\nComparing our equation with the standard equation, we can see that we have $h=-7$ and $k=1.$ Therefore, the coordinates of the vertex of the parabola are $(-7,1).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-115911/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9e302810-8b14-5c8c-8bbb-245386a66b7c"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-115911"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-115905/selection/77727aa61b22a39f9b5a87f27d06d281a4e8b5829fae0a32813ed2c63f4f29aa" :answer/id #uuid "ce0a65ad-fef1-58a8-841c-b6f690a46ef3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(-\\frac{1}{2},0)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-115905/selection/228d7b42fcb34515143bb5c9b68cc81052255c360fff1053199a2147dbd7eb12" :answer/id #uuid "18220b29-6dc6-5731-9065-7672676d1018" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(0,0)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-115905/selection/91d27013c76788268e2e33b95f23b5af7cdbb49f9e629538a767340569105ede" :answer/id #uuid "2d5e623c-58e9-57c5-bfac-8965c84d8dca" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(2,0)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-115905/selection/150d99653fc2555ef55da6bf23626f59964f3ca8ca854ad3e4e5141679d4b999" :answer/id #uuid "dc888568-12f2-55f5-8cc9-533dd4220c7b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(0,\\frac{1}{2})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-115905/selection/85cb4fac0396602d43dca2c00e3ca71b29816b8e6c6a13d1cfa7f3ced25f7b78" :answer/id #uuid "7fc77981-422e-5f9e-8088-dac591901b2d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(0,2)" :db/ensure [